     "text": "{\"reachable\": true, \"rationale\": \"The target is still reachable through edge0:reach -> h2_1:traverse -> h4_3:obtain -> crown:obtain. edge0:reach is an entry foothold. h2_1:traverse is an OR step, so edge0:reach alone is enough to reach it even with h1_1:access blocked. h4_3:obtain is an OR step whose only parent is h2_1:traverse, so it is reachable. crown:obtain is an OR step that needs only h4_3:obtain. The blocks do cut the other route: with h1_1:access blocked, h3_3:reach and h4_0:access cannot be reached. Blocking h3_0:traverse does not affect this path.\"}"
